export const NEWS_SEED_EMBEDDED: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "discord-guild-chat-linking.md": "---\ntitle: \"Discord Account Linking and Guild Chat Mirroring Come to WoW and Forever\"\nslug: discord-guild-chat-linking\ndate: 2026-11-11\nsummary: \"Modern WoW and WoW: Forever support Discord account linking and two-way guild chat mirroring for players and officers.\"\ntags:\n  - discord\n  - guilds\n  - midnight\n  - wow-forever\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24296228/stay-connected-in-world-of-warcraft-with-discord\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly\n---\n\nBlizzard has added official Discord account linking and guild chat mirroring to both modern World of Warcraft and World of Warcraft: Forever. Messages can travel between a linked Discord channel and in-game guild chat, so raid calls, PvP recruiting, and casual guild talk can continue when some members are logged out.\n\nThe feature is opt-in. Nothing is mirrored until a player connects a Discord account, and a guild channel is not linked until a guild leader or an officer with the right permissions sets it up.\n\n## Link your own account first\n\nIn game, open the Game Menu (Escape), go to Options, and open the Social tab. A new control, Enable Discord Functionality, starts the connection. You will leave the client briefly to confirm the link, so you should already be signed in to Discord.\n\nIf a player has not linked an account, their in-game messages do not appear in the Discord channel. Linked messages are visually distinct from ordinary guild chat, so you can see which side a line came from and put Discord traffic on the chat tabs you already use.\n\nYou can also choose the name that appears when a Discord message shows up in game:\n\n- **Default**, which currently uses the last online character\n- **Last Online Character Name**, using the last character on your Battle.net account that is in that guild\n- **Discord Global Name**, using your Discord global name\n\n## What guild leaders need to do\n\nOn the Discord side, the target channel must allow the people who will complete the link to Manage Channels, View Channel, and Send Messages.\n\nIn World of Warcraft, a guild leader or an eligible officer then:\n\n1. Opens the Guild & Communities UI (default hotkey J).\n2. Selects the Roster tab.\n3. Opens Guild Settings.\n4. Chooses Discord Settings under the Guild Control dropdown.\n5. Picks a Discord server they belong to, selects a linkable channel, and confirms the link.\n\nFrom there, guild leaders can keep Discord traffic in regular `/guild` chat or send it to a dedicated `/discord` channel. You can also create a separate Discord chat as its own channel inside the game.\n\nBlizzard also covered the feature in the WoW Weekly recap that followed Forever’s launch. Setup is the same in spirit on Midnight and Forever, even though the two games use different default interfaces.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThis is a first-party Blizzard feature. MagguuUI does not need to provide the link, and you should not look for a third-party Discord bridge if the official one already covers your guild. After you enable it, check your chat tabs so mirrored lines are visible and not hidden by a filter. If your guild leader routes traffic into a dedicated `/discord` channel, add that channel to a tab you actually watch. Custom chat layouts in MagguuUI or other addons should pick up the new channel the same way they pick up any other official chat type; no extra addon update is required just to turn the feature on.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Stay Connected in World of Warcraft with Discord](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24296228/stay-connected-in-world-of-warcraft-with-discord) — Blizzard News\n- [The Adventure Begins in WoW: Forever, Stay Connected with Discord, and Taldramir Takes Shape in WoW Weekly](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly) — Blizzard News\n",
  "echoes-of-the-worldcore-december-1.md": "---\ntitle: \"Midnight: Echoes of the Worldcore Arrives December 1\"\nslug: echoes-of-the-worldcore-december-1\ndate: 2026-11-13\nsummary: \"Echoes of the Worldcore goes live December 1 with regional maintenance, bringing Return to Dornogal, Talebound, and Lorewalking.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - echoes-of-the-worldcore\n  - talebound\n  - lorewalking\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317679/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-arrives-on-december-1\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24310659/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-overview\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24298591/world-of-warcraft-midnight-whats-next-panel-recap\n---\n\nBlizzard will release Midnight’s next content update, **Echoes of the Worldcore**, on December 1, 2026, with regional maintenance. An earlier overview had placed the update on the Public Test Realm without a live date; the December 1 announcement supersedes that. A later patch, **Eclipse**, remains officially announced as Midnight’s final major content update, still without a calendar date.\n\n## Return to Dornogal\n\nThe official preview sends players back to Dornogal. Xal’atath has breached the Worldcore, and the damaged Coreway is the way through. The new campaign, “The Return to Dornogal,” has players helping Arator, Brinthe, Dagran, and Brann find a path forward.\n\n## Talebound, Lorewalking, and Timeways\n\n**Talebound** arrives with this update as a new PvE action RPG mode. You are pulled into the tales of a mysterious Storyteller, solo or with friends, through enemies, bosses, puzzles, treasure, and relics. A separate official post covers the four stories, classes, and Quillgrave vendors in more detail; that mode also goes live on December 1.\n\n**Lorewalking** adds four topics for level 10 and above, started with Apprentice Lorewalker Li Li Stormstout in Stormwind, Orgrimmar, or Silvermoon City: Jaina, Thrall, the Titans, and Tyr. You can ask questions in the Lorewalking UI, leave or pause a story, and repeat it. Starting a different story before you finish one resets progress, and other quests cannot be progressed while Lorewalking is active.\n\n**Turbulent Timeways** starts when Echoes of the Worldcore launches and lasts eight weeks. The Markeet of the Infinite skyriding mount comes from “Master of the Turbulent Timeways VI,” earned by maintaining “Mastery of the Timeways” for any four weeks. A Timewalking dungeon grants Knowledge of the Timeways, a 5% stacking buff; after four dungeons it becomes Mastery of Timeways, granting 30% experience for the buff’s duration. Timewalking vendors receive new housing decor, and Aethas Sunreaver’s Timewalking quests in Silvermoon City offer increased rewards for a limited time, including a Heroic-level Cache of Quel’Thalas Treasures.\n\nThe Omnium Folio also expands, with two additional Motes of Omnial Inquiry and two new runes: Empowerment and Critical Mass. Official notes say you can learn more about the Sunstrider Omnium from Magister Umbric, Grand Magister Rommath, or Custodian Veldharin in the Lycaneum on the Isle of Quel’Danas.\n\n## Later, still announced: Eclipse and Season 3\n\nThe BlizzCon 2026 What’s Next panel described Eclipse as the final major Midnight update, a confrontation with Xal’atath and the Devouring Host. Announced features include a new zone, the Mantle Vault, and new allies, the Thraegar; a three-boss dungeon, Thraegar’s Stand, that will enter the Season 3 Mythic+ pool; an eight-boss raid, the Worldcore, source of Midnight’s Edge, the first Legendary of Midnight and of the Worldsoul Saga (a caster dagger; defeating the raid is only one unlock step); and a Lair boss, Noctinaxx, in the Gearhold.\n\nSeason 3 begins shortly after Eclipse launches. Its announced Mythic+ pool is Thraegar’s Stand, Magisters’ Terrace, Maisara Cavern, The Underrot, Iron Docks, Sanguine Depths, The Stonecore, and Uldaman: Legacy of Tyr. Top 1% and a new top 5% reward will be judged by specialization, not overall rating. Forsaken, Night Elf, and Troll characters will be able to become Paladins. No ship date has been published.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nWhen Echoes of the Worldcore reaches live realms on December 1, Talebound’s store is a first-party panel (character select, Game Menu, or Nib in Quillgrave) and does not need an addon. MagguuUI will not replace Talebound’s separate game mode. Lorewalking uses its own official UI under the minimap; leave that panel visible if you start a story, and do not expect a custom layout to track Lorewalking quest progress on its own.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Midnight: Echoes of the Worldcore Arrives on December 1](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317679/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-arrives-on-december-1) — Blizzard News\n- [Midnight: Echoes of the Worldcore Overview](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24310659/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-overview) — Blizzard News\n- [World of Warcraft: Midnight What’s Next Panel Recap](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24298591/world-of-warcraft-midnight-whats-next-panel-recap) — Blizzard News (Eclipse and Season 3 announcements)\n",
  "midnight-12-1-5-mid-season.md": "---\ntitle: \"Midnight 12.1.5 Brought Kith'ix, the Labyrinth, and Season 2's Mid-Season Refresh\"\nslug: midnight-12-1-5-mid-season\ndate: 2026-10-13\nsummary: \"Midnight's 12.1.5 update arrived October 13 with the Unbinding of Kith'ix, the Labyrinth of Kindo'jan, and Season 2 catch-up.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - patch-12-1-5\n  - season-2\n  - mythic-plus\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307306/midnight-s-12-1-5-content-update-is-now-live\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24304162/12-1-5-content-update-notes\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24295093/midnight-12-1-5-overview-new-adventures-await\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307310/hotfixes-november-6-2026\n  - https://www.wowhead.com/news/midnight-patch-12-1-5-releases-on-october-13th-world-of-warcraft-blizzard-news-383171\n---\n\nMidnight’s 12.1.5 content update arrived with weekly maintenance on October 13, 2026, in the Americas and October 14 in Europe. The patch continues the Quel’Thalas and Zul’Aman story, adds a single-boss raid and a large Delve-like Labyrinth, starts hourly Aqir Invasions, and rolls out mid-season catch-up for Season 2. Those systems remain the current mid-season content on live realms.\n\n## The Promise of Tomorrow and the Unbinding of Kith’ix\n\nThe campaign “The Promise of Tomorrow” follows Ula’tek’s defeat. Players work to steady an uneasy peace between Quel’Thalas and Zul’Aman, then descend the Coiled Isle to face the C’Thraxxi general Kith’ix.\n\nThe Unbinding of Kith’ix is a focused single-boss raid beneath the Venomous Abyss, with Story Mode, Raid Finder, Normal, Heroic, and Mythic in the official notes. Lady Liadrin accompanies the encounter. Mythic is a flexible 15–25 player fight.\n\n## Labyrinth of Kindo’jan\n\nThe Labyrinth of Kindo’jan is an ancient Amani funeral complex in Eversong Woods, north of Amani Pass. Blizzard describes it as a nine-chamber, mega-dungeon-style experience in the spirit of Delves, including a Tier 11 solo challenge, Mythic gear, cosmetics, and titles. Valeera Sanguinar is the companion. You can clear it in one sitting or wing by wing; a single wing still grants rewards, and later rooms raise both the loot and the risk. After the Chamber of Rites, the spirit guide Kinduru unlocks the rest of the complex for your Warband.\n\nStart via the campaign quest “The Long Way Around” to Liadrin above Thresh Cove, or “The Labyrinth” from Kul’amara the Fierce at Tokka’s Landing, then follow the line to Valeera.\n\n## Aqir Invasions and Keystone Myth\n\nAqir Invasions are zone-wide public events in Eversong or Zul’Aman. For ten minutes each hour, a sequence of public events leads into a boss fight. Each invasion has six scenario types — three combat-focused and three not — and combat scenarios can roll one of eight affixes. Rewards scale with how many objectives a group finishes before the window closes.\n\nKeystone Myth also returned in 12.1.5. The “Midnight Keystone Myth: Season 2” achievement requires a Mythic+ rating of 3,600. Blizzard also planned targeted tuning for outliers.\n\n## Mid-season power and later raid tuning\n\nOrin Straylight in Silvermoon City handles the mid-season catch-up. After “Umbral Blessings of the Catalyst,” you can trade gold, Voidlight Marl, or Veteran Mistcrests to him for one extra Nebulous Voidcore each week. During the week of October 20 he offered “Ascending with Venomstones.” Ten stones, used near the Catalyst in Silvermoon City, raise the item level of a fully upgraded Season 2 Hero, Myth, or maximum-quality Tidal Crafted weapon, trinket, or necklace. They drop from Heroic and Mythic raid bosses, +10 and higher keys, Tier 11 Bountiful Delves, and Nightmare Prey Champion chests. The weekly crest cap was also lifted that week.\n\nOn November 5 and 6, Blizzard reduced damage and health on several Venomous Abyss encounters. Ula’tek lost 15% health on Heroic, with tighter health scaling for smaller raids on Raid Finder through Heroic, and cuts to Unchecked Rage, Caustic Waves, and Malice. Earlier bosses, including Vashnik and the Coiled Altar, were also tuned down on Mythic. The patch also added optional minimap coordinates, raid-frame dispel indicators, a “Pulse Your Health” audio alert, and Warband-shared Legion and Battle for Azeroth reputations.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nIf you use MagguuUI on Midnight, check the new default minimap coordinates and raid-frame dispel options so they do not overlap displays your addon pack already shows. The Labyrinth, invasions, and raid do not need a special MagguuUI module; hide a default element only if it now duplicates something you already display.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Midnight's 12.1.5 Content Update is Now Live](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307306/midnight-s-12-1-5-content-update-is-now-live) — Blizzard News\n- [12.1.5 Content Update Notes](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24304162/12-1-5-content-update-notes) — Blizzard News\n- [Midnight 12.1.5 Overview: New Adventures Await](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24295093/midnight-12-1-5-overview-new-adventures-await) — Blizzard News\n- [Hotfixes: November 6, 2026](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307310/hotfixes-november-6-2026) — Blizzard News\n- [Midnight Patch 12.1.5 Releases on October 13th](https://www.wowhead.com/news/midnight-patch-12-1-5-releases-on-october-13th-world-of-warcraft-blizzard-news-383171) — Wowhead report of the official go-live announcement\n",
  "midnight-november-hotfixes-class-tuning.md": "---\ntitle: \"Midnight Hotfixes Buff Several Specs and Ease the Venomous Abyss\"\nslug: midnight-november-hotfixes-class-tuning\ndate: 2026-11-06\nauthor: Magguu\nsummary: \"Official Oct 27 class tuning and Nov 5–6 raid hotfixes buff several Midnight specs and ease Ula'tek and the Venomous Abyss.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - hotfixes\n  - class-tuning\n  - raid\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307310/hotfixes-november-6-2026\n---\n\nBlizzard’s live hotfix list for modern World of Warcraft was still headed November 6, 2026 as of November 19. It covers a late-October class pass and a further easing of The Venomous Abyss. The notes apply to Midnight alongside other versions of the game. Some changes go live immediately; others wait for a realm restart.\n\n## October 27 class tuning\n\nThe October 27 entry is the most recent PvE class pass in that list.\n\n- **Feral Druid:** all damage increased by 5%. This does not affect PvP.\n- **Restoration Druid:** Verdancy healing increased by 60%, Regrowth healing increased by 10%, and Improved Swiftmend now increases Swiftmend healing by 40%, up from 30%. These also do not affect PvP. Developers said the goal was to help Restoration handle burst damage in dungeons, where it was behind other healers, while leaving raid performance alone.\n- **Marksmanship Hunter:** Trick Shots now increases the ricochet damage of Aimed Shot and Rapid Fire by 85%, up from 75%. Explosive Shot and Volley damage each increased by 10%, to raise the spec’s area damage.\n- **Fire Mage:** all damage increased by 5% outside PvP.\n- **Affliction Warlock:** Unstable Affliction damage increased by 20% outside PvP.\n- **Destruction Warlock:** Rain of Fire damage increased by 20%.\n- **Subtlety Rogue:** all ability damage reduced by 8%. Trickster’s Fazed now increases damage by 5%, down from 7%. Developers said a compensation buff tied to patch 12.1.5 overshot, and that those patch changes had helped Trickster more than Deathstalker.\n\nMistweaver Monk received a fix so the Mistline talent more reliably heals the lowest-health target. A day earlier, Enhancement Shaman’s Voltaic Blaze was fixed when Ula’tek is the main target, and Affliction’s Cooldown Manager display for Summon Darkglare was corrected.\n\nThe same October 27 list also retunes several specs in PvP only, including a 5% Fire Mage damage reduction, Holy Paladin and Holy Priest healing increases, and buffs to Marksmanship and Dark Ranger, Devourer Demon Hunter, Frostfire Mage, and Restoration Shaman totems. Those PvP numbers do not change the PvE figures above.\n\n## November 5–6 raid easing\n\nOn November 5 and 6, Blizzard reduced damage and health across several Venomous Abyss encounters. On Mythic, Vashnik’s Malignance damage was cut by 37%, and its damage-over-time duration is now 16 seconds. Ula’tek lost 15% health on Heroic. Health scaling for Ula’tek and several adds was adjusted on Raid Finder, Normal, and Heroic so smaller raids are accounted for, and base health was lowered so larger groups do not push those values up.\n\nAbility damage was cut on all or most difficulties, including Unchecked Rage (61% on all difficulties), Caustic Waves, Malice, Virulent Spit, Falling Debris, and Viscous Echoes. Call of the Serpent summons fewer eggs on Normal and Heroic, Serpent’s Bite and Grasping Fangs hit fewer targets, and Phase 2 on Heroic now has eight eggs per side. Ula’tek no longer creates extra Caustic Waves from Spectral Tails during the Phase 3 wave walls on Heroic. Earlier bosses, including the Entombed Sentinels, Twin Fangs, and the Coiled Altar, were also tuned down, especially on Mythic.\n\nOctober 27 also fixed Labyrinth scenarios that were not granting Great Vault credit.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThese are combat and encounter changes, not a new interface patch. MagguuUI does not need an update for the damage and healing adjustments to apply. Review rotation notes for the buffed and nerfed specs, and note that several of the October 27 PvE changes explicitly do not affect PvP. The official Cooldown Manager fix for Summon Darkglare is already in the default UI.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Hotfixes: November 6, 2026](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307310/hotfixes-november-6-2026) — Blizzard News (rolling official list, including October 26–27 class notes and the November 5–6 raid changes)\n",
  "midnight-season-2-mythic-plus-pool.md": "---\ntitle: \"Midnight Season 2 Mythic+: The Official Dungeon Pool and Rewards\"\nslug: midnight-season-2-mythic-plus-pool\ndate: 2026-11-11\nauthor: Magguu\nsummary: \"Season 2's official Mythic+ pool is eight dungeons, including Altar of Fangs, with rating rewards through Keystone Myth.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - season-2\n  - mythic-plus\n  - dungeons\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24294369/midnight-season-2-is-now-live\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24293281/curse-of-ula-tek-content-update-notes\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307306/midnight-s-12-1-5-content-update-is-now-live\n---\n\nMidnight Season 2’s Mythic+ rotation is the current dungeon pool in modern World of Warcraft. Blizzard opened the eight-dungeon lineup on Heroic and Mythic 0 in the week of August 11, 2026, and started Mythic+ Season 2 in the week of August 18. Mythic 0 used a weekly lockout and dropped item level 292 gear in that first week, then moved to a daily reset when the season began, still at item level 292.\n\n## The official eight-dungeon pool\n\nThe Season 2 launch post and the Curse of Ula’tek notes list the same rotation:\n\n- **Altar of Fangs** (Midnight) — a new three-boss dungeon that entered the pool when Season 2 began\n- **Murder Row** (Midnight)\n- **Den of Nalorakk** (Midnight)\n- **The Blinding Vale** (Midnight)\n- **Voidscar Arena** (Midnight)\n- **Ruby Life Pools** (Dragonflight)\n- **Kings’ Rest** (Battle for Azeroth)\n- **Temple of Sethraliss** (Battle for Azeroth)\n\nThe Curse of Ula’tek notes describe the three returning dungeons as coming back with design and quality-of-life updates. Altar of Fangs was available up to Mythic 0 at the content update’s launch and joined Mythic+ a week later.\n\n## Seasonal rewards Blizzard has confirmed\n\nOfficial Season 2 Mythic+ rewards are tied to rating and end-of-season placement:\n\n- **Midnight Keystone Conqueror: Season 2** — a Feat of Strength and the title “the Venomous,” at a Mythic+ rating of at least 1,500\n- **Midnight Keystone Master: Season 2** — the Breath of Blight mount, at a rating of at least 2,000\n- **Midnight Keystone Legend: Season 2** — the Breath of Ruin mount, at a rating of at least 3,000\n- **Midnight Keystone Myth: Season 2** — listed with the title “the Venomous Contender.” The 12.1.5 content update set this achievement’s requirement at a Mythic+ rating of 3,600\n- **Venomous Champion: Midnight Season 2** — for finishing the season in the top 1% of Mythic+ rating in your region\n- **Venomous Hero: Midnight Season 2** — the title “the Venomous Hero,” for finishing in the top 0.1%\n\nTimed runs at Mythic 10 or higher also unlock a dungeon portal for each of the eight dungeons.\n\n## What official notes do not list\n\nBlizzard’s Season 2 launch article does not publish the weekly Mythic+ affix schedule, keystone breakpoints, or affix tooltips. Community guides describe a ladder that includes Lindormi’s Guidance and Xal’atath’s Bargain, but those details are not in the official Season 2 or Curse of Ula’tek posts cited here, so they are omitted. Check the in-game keystone and Group Finder for the affixes actually active on your key this week.\n\nThe mid-season 12.1.5 update also returned Keystone Myth and said Blizzard would apply targeted dungeon tuning for difficulty outliers. It did not replace the eight-dungeon pool.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThe Season 2 pool and portals are first-party systems. MagguuUI does not need a special module for the rotation to appear. After you time a +10, the official dungeon teleport is enough; you do not need an addon to add those portals. If you use a keystone or dungeon-timer plugin, confirm it still recognizes the current eight names, especially Altar of Fangs. Leave affix icons and routes to whatever the game and your plugins actually show this week, rather than to an unofficial schedule.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Midnight Season 2 is Now Live!](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24294369/midnight-season-2-is-now-live) — Blizzard News\n- [Curse of Ula'tek Content Update Notes](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24293281/curse-of-ula-tek-content-update-notes) — Blizzard News\n- [Midnight's 12.1.5 Content Update is Now Live](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24307306/midnight-s-12-1-5-content-update-is-now-live) — Blizzard News (Keystone Myth at 3,600)\n",
  "november-trading-post-sweet-tooth.md": "---\ntitle: \"November’s Trading Post Has a Sweet Tooth Theme and a Bunmover Mount\"\nslug: november-trading-post-sweet-tooth\ndate: 2026-11-01\nauthor: Magguu\nsummary: \"November's official Trading Post theme is Sweet Tooth. Fill the Traveler's Log to earn the Hot Motocross Bunmover 4600.\"\ntags:\n  - trading-post\n  - midnight\n  - events\n  - cosmetics\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316094/prepare-for-forever-try-midnights-talebound-and-discover-sweet-treats-in-wow-weekly\n---\n\nNovember’s Trading Post in modern World of Warcraft, still running as of November 19, is built around a **Sweet Tooth** theme. In an official WoW Weekly recap, Blizzard said this month is about “indulging your sweet side” and that the post is “serving up a sugar rush” of new collection items. The only reward named in that announcement is the monthly Traveler’s Log bonus: the **Hot Motocross Bunmover 4600** mount.\n\nBlizzard’s flavor text for the mount is: “When dessert manufacturing meets speed optimization. Intact bun delivery not guaranteed.”\n\n## How the official bonus works\n\nThe Bunmover 4600 is not described as a Trader’s Tender purchase. You earn it by completing Traveler’s Log activities and filling the monthly log. The Traveler’s Log lives in the Adventure Guide (the default shortcut is Shift-J). The same weekly post tells players to complete activities to earn Trader’s Tender and to fill the log to claim the bonus mount.\n\nBlizzard did not publish a full November catalog, individual Tender prices, or an exact end timestamp in that announcement. The in-game Trading Post is the place to see this month’s shop list and any countdown on the log. Unofficial item lists circulated after the preview; those prices and names are left out here because they were not in the official post.\n\n## Where to find the Trading Post\n\nThe official weekly names four locations:\n\n- **Stormwind:** T&W (Tawney and Wilder), just outside the Mage District\n- **Orgrimmar:** the Zen’shiri Trading Post, next to Grommash Hold\n- **Dornogal:** the Foregrounds, on the Isle of Dorn, where representatives of both shops are open\n- **Renewed Silvermoon City:** representatives of both Tawney and Wilder and the Zen’shiri Trading Post\n\nNew and returning Midnight players can also take Blizzard’s in-game Trading Post tour, which covers where the post is and how additional Trader’s Tender is earned through the Traveler’s Log.\n\nThe same weekly also promoted other November collectibles, including the Living Heartsbane Cauldron mount and the Grimtide Estate and Grimtide Decor housing packs. Those were not listed as Trading Post items in the announcement, so they should be checked in the shop or housing interface rather than assumed to be part of the Sweet Tooth catalog.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThe Trading Post, Traveler’s Log, and Collector’s Cache are first-party Midnight windows. MagguuUI does not grant Tender or the Bunmover mount, and you do not need an addon to claim the log reward. If a custom layout hides the Adventure Guide or vendor interaction, restore or keybind Shift-J and make sure the Stormwind, Orgrimmar, Dornogal, or Silvermoon vendors remain clickable so you can finish the November log before the month turns over.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Prepare for Forever, Try Midnight’s Talebound, and Discover Sweet Treats in WoW Weekly](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316094/prepare-for-forever-try-midnights-talebound-and-discover-sweet-treats-in-wow-weekly) — Blizzard News\n",
  "pouch-of-violet-dust-launch-celebration.md": "---\ntitle: \"The Pouch of Violet Dust Twitch Drop Has Ended\"\nslug: pouch-of-violet-dust-launch-celebration\ndate: 2026-11-12\nsummary: \"The Pouch of Violet Dust Twitch Drop for WoW: Forever closed November 12 at 4:30 p.m. PST. The toy is not being seeded as a live article.\"\ntags:\n  - wow-forever\n  - twitch-drops\n  - events\n  - camping\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317678/set-your-campfire-ablaze-with-the-pouch-of-violet-dust\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315820/world-of-warcraft-forever-now-live\n---\n\nThe launch-week Twitch Drop for World of Warcraft: Forever is over. From November 4 at 4:30 p.m. PST to November 12 at 4:30 p.m. PST (1:30 a.m. on November 13 in Europe/Berlin), watching eligible World of Warcraft streams could unlock the Pouch of Violet Dust, a temporary campfire toy. That watch window is closed, and this seed stays unpublished so the site does not present an ended drop as current.\n\n## What the toy does\n\nThe Pouch of Violet Dust is available only in WoW: Forever. It turns a campfire purple and extends all camp benefits by one hour, for a total duration of two hours. Once it is used, anyone resting at that camp receives the same longer duration.\n\nThe toy can be used only during the “WoW: Forever Launch Celebration.” Blizzard says that event period expires in early December. After that, the toy is removed from collections and is no longer available in game. The watch window that ended on November 12 and the later celebration expiry are separate dates. New drops can no longer be earned; players who already claimed the toy can still use it until the celebration ends.\n\nThe effect sits on top of Forever’s camping system. A Basic Campfire can become a shared campsite, nearby players can add up to three profession-crafted Camp Features (one each), and sitting or crafting there for at least one minute grants those benefits. The camp buffs are mutually exclusive with the corresponding class buffs.\n\n## How it was earned\n\nThe official drop required a linked Twitch and Battle.net account, four hours of eligible World of Warcraft content on Twitch while Drops were active, and a claim in Twitch’s Drops Inventory. Progress could move from channel to channel in the World of Warcraft category; watching more than one channel at once did not speed it up. After a claim, the first Battle.net region entered received the item, with up to 24 hours for delivery. Unclaimed rewards expired seven days after they were claimed if no Battle.net account was linked.\n\nA YouTube path was also documented: link Battle.net through YouTube Connected Apps and watch the official World of Warcraft channel for the full time.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThe pouch is a first-party Forever toy, not an addon item, and MagguuUI does not need to display or grant it. If you already have it, use it at a campfire the same way you would use any other toy until the celebration ends in early December. Camp benefits and class buffs do not stack when they correspond to one another, which is a game rule rather than a UI setting.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Set Your Campfire Ablaze with the Pouch of Violet Dust!](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317678/set-your-campfire-ablaze-with-the-pouch-of-violet-dust) — Blizzard News\n- [WoW Weekly: The Adventure Begins in WoW: Forever](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly) — Blizzard News\n- [World of Warcraft: Forever Now Live!](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315820/world-of-warcraft-forever-now-live) — Blizzard News (camping system)\n",
  "taldramir-the-whispering-wood.md": "---\ntitle: \"Taldramir, the Whispering Wood, Is Forever’s First Legendary\"\nslug: taldramir-the-whispering-wood\ndate: 2026-11-05\nsummary: \"Blizzard introduced Taldramir, the Whispering Wood, as World of Warcraft: Forever’s first legendary, forged with Wētā Workshop.\"\ntags:\n  - wow-forever\n  - legendary\n  - taldramir\n  - blizzard\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317865/wow-forever-watch-forging-forever\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly\n  - https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/taldramir-the-whispering-wood-revealed-as-wow-forever-legendary-383747\n---\n\nBlizzard has introduced **Taldramir, the Whispering Wood**, as World of Warcraft: Forever’s first legendary, in a “Forging Forever” feature and the WoW Weekly recap that followed launch. Official copy describes the weapon as forged by Wētā Workshop and wielded by adventurers in Forever.\n\nThat is as far as the official posts go. Blizzard has not published stats, effects, class or specialization restrictions, or a method for obtaining the weapon. This note does not fill those gaps from datamining or comment speculation.\n\nWowhead’s report, cited as a secondary source, identifies the reveal model as a two-handed staff with a clear Druid theme and notes that the weapon also appears in Skyborne key art. Treat those observations as Wowhead’s, not as official item tooltip data.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nUntil Blizzard publishes how the legendary is obtained and what it does, there is nothing for a MagguuUI pack to surface beyond ordinary item tooltips once the weapon exists on a character. Do not expect an addon to track an unpublished acquisition path. When official acquisition notes appear, they will belong in a later article, not in a guessed tracker.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WoW: Forever – Watch Forging Forever](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317865/wow-forever-watch-forging-forever) — Blizzard News\n- [The Adventure Begins in WoW: Forever, Stay Connected with Discord, and Taldramir Takes Shape in WoW Weekly](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly) — Blizzard News\n- [Taldramir, the Whispering Wood Revealed as WoW: Forever Legendary](https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/taldramir-the-whispering-wood-revealed-as-wow-forever-legendary-383747) — Wowhead\n",
  "talebound-twisted-tales-december-1.md": "---\ntitle: \"Talebound’s Twisted Tales and Deadly Fates Arrive December 1\"\nslug: talebound-twisted-tales-december-1\ndate: 2026-11-12\nsummary: \"Talebound, Midnight’s PvE action RPG mode, goes live December 1 with four stories, three classes, and rewards spent in Quillgrave.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - talebound\n  - echoes-of-the-worldcore\n  - cosmetics\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316569/talebounds-twisted-tales-and-deadly-fates-arrive-december-1\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317679/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-arrives-on-december-1\n---\n\nTalebound, Midnight’s new PvE action RPG mode, arrives on December 1, 2026, with regional maintenance, alongside Echoes of the Worldcore. You play as part of a mysterious Storyteller’s macabre chronicles, solo or with friends, through themed tales on Normal, Veteran, and Heroic difficulties.\n\n## From Red Hollow to Quillgrave\n\nThe official overview starts the journey in Red Hollow, on a darkened road that leads to the Storyteller and then to Quillgrave, the lantern-lit village used as a hub between runs. After each tale, you return to work with four vendors: the Arcanist (potions, draughts, and flasks found in the tale), the Scribe (talents and abilities), the Antiquarian (passives that change how a tale can be approached), and the Outfitter (starting health, damage, energy, and focus).\n\nFour stories are listed, each with its own setting and bosses:\n\n- **Darkhaven**, home to Konrad von Sonnesheim, the Lord Marshal, and Alexandre Dozsenc, the Blood Bishop, after a plague has isolated the town\n- **Greenthistle Wood**, around the villages of Shady Hollow and Riverton, with two witches, a giant, and other fiends\n- **Greywake’s Expedition**, following losses to Zzyg’th, the Hadal Tyrant, and Chathoa, the Herald from Beyond\n- **Grove of the Night Court**, a chronicle of Tilywth, the Fairy Queen, and Maernok, the Nightmare King\n\nCollections of these stories are also available in town if you want to hear them again.\n\n## Classes, movement, and rewards\n\nEvery class can double jump, dodge, Evade (a brief window of immunity), Sprint, and Guard. You choose one of three archetypes, each with a talent tree of 27 points. Tales of Valor spent at the Scribe unlock extra abilities and later upgrade those talents.\n\n- **Witch** leans on lightning, poison, spiders, moonlight, thorns, and ravens.\n- **Slayer** mixes a sword with a gun and monster-hunter tools.\n- **Inquisitor** uses holy and fire attacks, including several spells that can be used while moving.\n\nProgression currency includes Ducats, which convert into the resources used to advance in Talebound, and Bound Silver, spent on transmog sets, individual pieces, and other cosmetics in the Talebound store. That store is available from the character selection screen, the Game Menu, or Nib in Quillgrave. Official reward art shown with the announcement includes the Witch Hunter’s Shadow Attire set, a Shadowbound Storybook mount, and Quillgrave housing decor.\n\nTo start, open Talebound from the World of Warcraft menu, create a hero, and choose an archetype. After the Red Hollow introduction and a first look at Quillgrave, you pick a story and a difficulty.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nTalebound is a first-party game mode with its own vendors, talent panel, and store. MagguuUI will not replace those windows or grant Bound Silver. When the mode goes live on December 1, use the official menu entry to start it, and keep the in-mode UI visible rather than expecting a Retail layout to cover Quillgrave or the Talebound store.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Talebound’s Twisted Tales and Deadly Fates Arrive December 1](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316569/talebounds-twisted-tales-and-deadly-fates-arrive-december-1) — Blizzard News\n- [Midnight: Echoes of the Worldcore Arrives on December 1](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24317679/midnight-echoes-of-the-worldcore-arrives-on-december-1) — Blizzard News\n",
  "wow-22nd-anniversary-celebration.md": "---\ntitle: \"World of Warcraft’s 22nd Anniversary Runs November 17 to December 8\"\nslug: wow-22nd-anniversary-celebration\ndate: 2026-11-17\nsummary: \"The 22nd Anniversary event is in the Caverns of Time from November 17 to December 8, with XP and reputation buffs and Warband-wide rewards.\"\ntags:\n  - midnight\n  - anniversary\n  - events\n  - cosmetics\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316098/join-the-world-of-warcraft-22nd-anniversary-celebration\n---\n\nWorld of Warcraft’s 22nd Anniversary celebration runs from November 17 to December 8, 2026, in the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. Holiday Celebrants offer a quest, and portals in Orgrimmar and Stormwind provide a ride to the event grounds.\n\nPlayers receive an automatic 10% experience and reputation buff during the event. Completing the repeatable “Celebrate Good Fun!” quest from Yllana in Tanaris each day adds another 10%. The anniversary buff also stacks with other experience and reputation increases. The official post lists a 25% experience buff from the Five Warband Mentors: Midnight achievement, a 15% experience and gold bonus from War Mode, and a 10% bonus from the Draught of Ten Lands potion for characters level 49 and lower. Together, the two anniversary bonuses are a 20% experience and reputation increase from the event itself.\n\n## Currency, vendors, and the Loyal Watchman set\n\nActivities award currencies that can be spent on the grounds, including Timewarped Badges from Timewalking events, Marks of Honor exchanged for legacy weapons and armor at PvP vendors, Ancient Mana, and Polished Pet Charms. Officially named vendors include:\n\n- **Traeya**, selling Tier 2 armor for Timewarped Badges\n- **Time-Displaced Thanthaldis Snowgleam** and **Time-Displaced Jorek Ironside**, selling scaling PvP-themed weapons and armor for Marks of Honor and Timewarped Badges\n- **Historian Ma’di**, the anniversary rewards vendor, for Timewarped Badges\n- **Notary Grably**, for Bronze Celebration titles\n\nThe official reward example is the Loyal Watchman ensemble: helm, gauntlets, trousers, cuirass, spaulders, belt, and boots.\n\nQuests and activity completions are tracked Warband-wide. They can be finished on any character in the Warband and count toward the weekly amount of Warband Transferable Tokens the Warband can earn. There is no requirement to run the event on multiple characters each week unless you want to.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThe anniversary grounds, vendors, and daily quest are first-party event UI. MagguuUI does not need a special module for the buffs or the Loyal Watchman set to be available. If a custom layout hides holiday NPCs, the Tanaris portals, or the vendor windows, restore those interactions before December 8 so daily “Celebrate Good Fun!” and the weekly token cap remain reachable.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Join the World of Warcraft 22nd Anniversary Celebration](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316098/join-the-world-of-warcraft-22nd-anniversary-celebration) — Blizzard News\n",
  "wow-forever-november-hotfixes.md": "---\ntitle: \"WoW: Forever Hotfixes Through November 17 Restore UBRS and Keep Tuning Classes\"\nslug: wow-forever-november-hotfixes\ndate: 2026-11-17\nsummary: \"The official Forever hotfix list, updated through November 17, restores UBRS difficulty, adjusts camping and Priest healing, and keeps earlier class changes.\"\ntags:\n  - wow-forever\n  - hotfixes\n  - class-tuning\n  - pvp\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315281/wow-forever-hotfixes-november-17-2026\n  - https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/pvp-faction-balance-updates-november-10/2408781\n  - https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/warlock-and-hunter-class-tuning-now-live-in-wow-forever-383826\n  - https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/blizzard-buffs-dungeon-enemy-experience-gains-383808\n---\n\nBlizzard’s official World of Warcraft: Forever hotfix list is a rolling document. As of November 17, 2026, it still includes the launch-week dungeon experience and class changes, and it adds later fixes for camping, Upper Blackrock Spire, and several class and item issues.\n\n## November 16–17\n\nOn November 17, Mounted players can no longer sleep in the Cozy Sleeping Bag while saddled. The bag can now be placed in specific locations, similar to hunter traps, and it provides a Resting aura when you are inside its area of effect. Might of Stormwind and Warchief's Blessing now cancel correctly on death and are no longer applied to non-players. A Shaman bug that made Flurry drop stacks when Windfury Totem attacks landed was fixed.\n\nUpper Blackrock Spire had been running with enemy health and damage significantly lower than intended. The November 17 notes restore the intended difficulty and say a full, attentive group is required again.\n\nItem and set corrections the same day include letting Shadow Priests hold a Night Watchman's Torch, fixing range and damage on Escape Plan, and giving Whiteout Staff and Crackling Staff matching stats (25 Stamina, 25 Intellect, and 74 Spell Power from weapon damage). Soulforge Armor, the upgraded dungeon set for Paladin tanks, now has Spell Power instead of Strength. Blizzard said it wants Paladin tanks to favor Spell Power as their primary damage stat.\n\nThe November 16 notes include a scheduled weekly-maintenance change for Priests: Vampiric Embrace healing is based on 10% of the Shadow damage done by the casting Priest, down from 20%, and the caster receives 100% increased healing from that effect. Developers said solo play is unchanged. Other November 16 fixes cover Windfury Totem attacks incorrectly ignoring armor and missing an internal cooldown, Rogue poison ranks exceeding the cap, and Druid Wild Growth cooldown and Genesis issues.\n\n## Earlier in November: dungeon experience, classes, and PvP creation\n\nOn November 9, experience awarded for all enemy kills in dungeons increased by 50%, so repeat runs are more worthwhile after launch tuning had left much of a dungeon’s value in the quests.\n\nNovember 10’s class changes remain on the official list. Enhancement Shaman saw the largest redesign: Stormstrike is 100% weapon damage, down from 150%, with an 8-second cooldown, up from 6. Mental Dexterity’s Intellect-to-Attack Power conversion is 33/66/100%, down from 50/100/150%. Maelstrom Weapon now grants 20% reduced cast time and mana cost per application at every rank, and its activation rate scales with talent rank. Blizzard said beta changes had pushed Enhancement toward Spell Power and Intellect, and that it wants Windfury to remain at the heart of the specialization. Weapon imbues and weapon totems can be used together, so Windfury Weapon and Windfury Totem both apply.\n\nHunter pets that mistakenly had 150% of normal health were corrected to 115%. Arcane Shot and Beast Mastery’s Summon Hawk now cost a flat 11% of base mana at every rank. Hawk melee damage was increased by about 80%. Affliction Warlock’s Wrack no longer boosts periodic damage by a percentage; its own damage was reduced by 30%, and while it is channeled, Siphon Life, Corruption, and Bane of Agony tick 100% faster.\n\nWith realm restarts on November 10, the Auction House minimum deposit became 1 copper, down from 1 silver. On the same day, Community Manager Kaivax wrote that PvP rulesets need closer faction balance than a worst-case split of roughly 55/45. Character creation becomes increasingly difficult on the more populous faction — at the time, Horde on North American PvP rulesets and Alliance on EU Roleplay-PvP — and those restrictions can flip as populations shift.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nThese hotfixes change combat math, a few default Cooldown Manager entries, and some world and item bugs. They do not require a new addon version by themselves. Update rotation notes for Enhancement, Hunter mana costs, Affliction Wrack, and the Vampiric Embrace change if you play those specs. Auction House, mail, camping placement, and PvP creation limits are not UI settings.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WoW: Forever Hotfixes - November 17, 2026](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315281/wow-forever-hotfixes-november-17-2026) — Official rolling hotfix list\n- [PvP Faction Balance Updates - November 10](https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/pvp-faction-balance-updates-november-10/2408781) — Official forum post by Kaivax\n- [Warlock and Hunter Class Tuning Now Live in WoW: Forever](https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/warlock-and-hunter-class-tuning-now-live-in-wow-forever-383826) — Wowhead\n- [Blizzard Buffs Dungeon Enemy Experience Gains](https://www.wowhead.com/forever/news/blizzard-buffs-dungeon-enemy-experience-gains-383808) — Wowhead\n",
  "wow-forever-now-live.md": "---\ntitle: \"World of Warcraft: Forever Launched November 4\"\nslug: wow-forever-now-live\ndate: 2026-11-04\nsummary: \"WoW: Forever launched worldwide on November 4, 2026, with new zones, the Skyborne, rulesets, and a first-login interface preset.\"\ntags:\n  - wow-forever\n  - launch\n  - blizzard\n  - skyborne\nsources:\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315820/world-of-warcraft-forever-now-live\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24302093/carve-a-new-path-with-world-of-warcraft-forever\n  - https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly\n---\n\nWorld of Warcraft: Forever launched worldwide on November 4, 2026, at 3:00 p.m. PST (midnight, November 5, in Europe/Berlin). Blizzard positions it as a permanent game alongside modern World of Warcraft and existing Classic versions. Access is included with an active World of Warcraft subscription or Game Time.\n\nThe setting sits after *Warcraft III Reforged: Forsaken Kingdom* and before Molten Core. Players level to 60 across the original continents, then continue through new stories and ongoing updates.\n\n## New ground in a familiar world\n\nEastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor are expanded with new and reimagined zones and more than 1,000 new quests from levels 1 to 60. Official destinations include:\n\n- **Mount Hyjal**, set after Archimonde’s defeat, including Darkwhisper Gorge.\n- **Shen’dralas**, a previously hidden area between Mulgore and Desolace, tied to the Shen’dralar, Eldre’Thalas, Dire Maul, and nearby centaur tribes.\n- **The Riverglades**, a mid-30s to mid-40s frontier with more than 150 new quests.\n- **Zephras Isle**, a level 1–12 starting experience with Classic-style presentation and architecture inspired by Skywall.\n\n## Skyborne and new class combinations\n\nThe Skyborne — also called the shen’dorei, or “hidden people” — are a new playable race. Their story begins on Zephras Isle. At character creation you choose a faction: Horde-aligned Windshapers can become Shaman, and Alliance-aligned High-Order Skyborne can become Mages.\n\nForever also opens class combinations that were not available in original World of Warcraft, including Orc Mages, Troll Warlocks, Undead Paladins, Human Hunters, Gnome Priests, and Dwarf Shamans.\n\n## Presets, rulesets, and names\n\nThe first time you log in, Forever asks you to choose an Experience Preset before you pick a Ruleset. **Classic** starts with standard-definition models, quest helpers off, one-bag and transmog off, camera-turning binds, and a Classic screen UI layout. **Enhanced** starts with high-definition models, those helpers on, one-bag and transmog on, strafe binds, and a centralized UI layout. Blizzard recommends Enhanced if you are unsure. The preset is only a starting point; options can be changed later under Game Menu > Options, and the preset screen does not return after the first login. Model definition can also be chosen per character and changed later in Options or at a Barbershop.\n\nInstead of a traditional realm list, you choose a Ruleset: Normal, PvP, Roleplay, or Roleplay PvP. Each is a broader player ecosystem rather than a single realm. A Hardcore ruleset is planned for sometime after launch; no date has been published. Character names use a two-part structure so a full name is unique within a region.\n\n## Systems around the journey\n\nA camping system turns the Cooking profession’s Basic Campfire into a shared campsite. Nearby players can add up to three profession-crafted Camp Features (one each). Sitting or crafting there for at least one minute grants those benefits, which are mutually exclusive with the corresponding class buffs.\n\nThe Legacy System is an account-wide horizontal track with Challenges, Perks, and Rewards. Leveling alts is encouraged but not required; advantages can be unlocked on a single character. Forever also ships gamepad support for targeting, casting, looting, and menus.\n\n## What this means for your UI / MagguuUI\n\nMagguuUI maintains a separate Forever flavor, kept distinct from the Retail (Midnight) pack. Choose the Classic or Enhanced preset first so the default Blizzard layout matches how you want the built-in UI to behave, then load MagguuUI. Those options remain under Game Menu > Options after the preset screen is gone. Gamepad support is first-party; a desktop addon pack will not replace it, so gamepad users should confirm targeting, menus, and bags still work with their layout enabled.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [World of Warcraft: Forever Now Live!](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24315820/world-of-warcraft-forever-now-live) — Blizzard News\n- [Carve a New Path with World of Warcraft: Forever](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24302093/carve-a-new-path-with-world-of-warcraft-forever) — Blizzard News (launch time and subscription access)\n- [WoW Weekly: The Adventure Begins in WoW: Forever](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24316097/the-adventure-begins-in-wow-forever-stay-connected-with-discord-and-taldramir-takes-shape-in-wow-weekly) — Blizzard News\n"
}
